join Timot leftmost [animation="Slide In" length="0.3"]
Timot: MOVE! NOW!

join Brimble rightmost [animation="Slide In" length="0.3"]
Brimble: HISSS!

Timot: (grabbing your arm, yanking you down the path) They broke the gate at dawn—the town's being overrun!

Timot: (stops abruptly, breathless, sizing you up) Wait. You can fight?

Timot: Thank Aurethiel. Then listen fast\:

Timot: Joystick—left stick moves, right aims, trigger fires.
Timot: Keyboard—W-A-S-D moves, left click attacks. Hit ESC to pause the game.
Timot: Mobile—left touch moves, right touch aims and fires.

Timot: Stay mobile. Stop moving and you're dead. Simple as that. Defend the town and buy time us time while the villagers flee to the safe zones. There are a hundred villagers that we need to evacuate. If you have the coin, come to my shop in the northwest corner of town for upgrades and defenses.

Brimble: Meow! (frantic, clawing at Timot's cloak)

Timot: Not now, Brimble!

Timot: (back to you) Creatures of The Moribund Order—pouring in from every direction.

Timot: Necromancers. Death knights. Things that shouldn't walk.

Timot: They want the village. They want the people.

Timot: We don't know why. We just know they can't have them.

Timot: We're evacuating but we need time.

Timot: That's you. You're the time.

Timot: (pulls a glowing vial from his cloak) See this? Speed. Strength. Fire in a bottle.

Timot: My shop's open—kill monsters, take their coin, buy survival.

Timot: Every second you hold them, another villager escapes.

join Narrator rightmost
Narrator: A roar tears through the valley. The ground shakes. Steel rings against steel in the distance.
leave Narrator

Timot: (voice drops) Annadaeus warned us this would come. Back when we thought we were safe.
Timot: She sang of the storm before any of us could see the clouds.

Timot: (slight smile, grim but defiant) If we survive this… maybe she'll sing of our victory too.

Brimble: MEOW! (sharp, desperate)

Timot: Fine! Go! Back to the shop!
leave Brimble

Timot: (grips your shoulder, fear and steel in his eyes) This is it, hero.
Timot: Lumora stands or falls on what you do next.

Timot: You're the light now.
join Narrator rightmost

Narrator: The screams grow louder. Closer.
leave Narrator

Timot: (releases you, steps back) Make them remember why they fear the dawn.
